E["npc:archmage-alturus"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Alturus",z="deadwind",s="Archmage Alturus is a senior Kirin Tor investigator stationed outside the haunting towers of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Representing the Violet Eye, he monitors the volatile magical ley-lines converging upon the former seat of the Guardian Medivh. Travelers seeking to uncover the dark secrets of the tower must first consult his careful observations.",h="Archmage Alturus is a senior Kirin Tor investigator stationed outside the haunting towers of Karazhan in...",sec={{t="Watcher of the Tower",b="While most scholars of Dalaran avoid the desolate ravines of Deadwind Pass, Archmage Alturus remains encamped in the shadow of Karazhan. Representing the secretive Violet Eye, Alturus is tasked by his peers with measuring the arcane disturbances and restless spirits haunting the surrounding ruins. He understands better than most that Karazhan sits directly atop a massive nexus where Azeroth's magical ley-lines converge, making its residual corruption a threat to the entire world.",sp=0},{t="Studies in the Cellar",b="Alturus's vigilance extends beyond passive observation. With access to a secluded sanctum hidden near the Master's Cellar, he tirelessly inspects the grounds for traces of Medivh's lingering sorcery and otherworldly intruders. He often enlists capable adventurers to recover relics, chart ghostly disturbances, and piece together Medivh's lost writings, desperate to prevent the tower's unbridled power from slipping into worse hands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Alturus?",a="Archmage Alturus is a high-ranking human mage of Dalaran and an operative of the Violet Eye. He is stationed in Deadwind Pass just outside the gates of Karazhan to study and contain the bizarre magical phenomena emanating from the citadel.",al={"who is alturus","archmage alturus lore","alturus karazhan"}},{q="Why is Alturus standing outside Karazhan?",a="He is monitoring the arcane instability of Karazhan. Because the tower sits directly over a critical convergence of Azeroth's subterranean ley-lines, any magical catastrophe within could have catastrophic consequences for the rest of the continent.",al={"why is alturus in deadwind","alturus purpose","what is alturus doing"}},{q="What is the Violet Eye?",a="The Violet Eye is a secretive sect of the Kirin Tor dedicated exclusively to watching Karazhan and its master, Medivh. Even after Medivh's fall, they maintain their vigil around the tower to ensure its dark powers remain contained.",al={"who are the violet eye","violet eye faction","dalaran violet eye"}},{q="Does Alturus work alone?",a="Alturus coordinates with fellow Kirin Tor researchers sent to Deadwind Pass, including Archmage Leryda, and reports back to senior authorities in Dalaran such as Archmage Cedric.",al={"who is alturus with","alturus allies","alturus camp"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, Alturus represents the Kirin Tor's enduring vigil over Medivh's unchecked ambition and the volatile nexus beneath Karazhan.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though operating under Dalaran's neutral scholarly banner, Alturus provides human and Alliance travelers with vital insight into the growing perils of southern Deadwind Pass."},kw={"alturus","archmage alturus","deadwind pass","karazhan","kirin tor","master's cellar","medivh","violet eye"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","subzone:master-s-cellar","npc:archmage-leryda","topic:medivh","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Archmage Alturus"}}
E["npc:archmage-leryda"] = {t="npc",n="Archmage Leryda",z="deadwind",s="Archmage Leryda is a Kirin Tor sorceress and senior operative of the Violet Eye stationed outside the haunted tower of Karazhan. Working alongside Archmage Alturus, she monitors the supernatural anomalies stirring within Medivh's abandoned estate and enlists capable adventurers to delve into its depths.",h="Archmage Leryda is a Kirin Tor sorceress and senior operative of the Violet Eye stationed outside the haunted...",sec={{t="Watcher of the Tower",b="Perched at the threshold of Karazhan in the blighted expanse of Deadwind Pass, Archmage Leryda represents the watchful gaze of Dalaran. The Violet Eye—a covert sect of the Kirin Tor dedicated exclusively to observing Karazhan and the legacy of the Last Guardian—maintains a constant post here. While the tower has long been shuttered, sinister energies and restless spirits have begun to pulse from its halls once more. Leryda acts as a primary liaison for those venturing into the spire, outfitting brave champions with specialized signets that channel the power and discipline of the Violet Eye across various combat paths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Archmage Leryda?",a="Archmage Leryda is an archmage of Dalaran and a ranking member of the Violet Eye stationed outside Karazhan in Deadwind Pass.",al={"leryda","who is leryda","archmage leryda lore"}},{q="What is the Violet Eye?",a="The Violet Eye is a secretive order formed by the Kirin Tor specifically tasked with surveilling Medivh, his tower of Karazhan, and the dangerous magical fallout left in the wake of his demise.",al={"violet eye","who are the violet eye","kirin tor violet eye"}},{q="Why is she standing outside Karazhan?",a="Leryda observes the dark energies stirring inside the abandoned tower, assisting expeditionary forces and recognizing the achievements of those who combat the threats within Karazhan.",al={"why is leryda here","leryda purpose","what does leryda do"}},{q="What are the rings she offers?",a="She bestows the Violet Signet to adventurers aligned with the Violet Eye. These enchanted rings honor martial disciplines such as the assassin, protector, restorer, or mage, growing in power as a hero earns greater standing with the order.",al={"violet signet","karazhan ring","leryda rings"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Kirin Tor archmage, Leryda respects fellow practitioners of the arcane who possess the courage to confront the unstable remnants of the Guardian's grand magic."},kw={"archmage leryda","deadwind pass","karazhan","kirin tor","leryda","violet eye","violet signet"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","npc:archmage-alturus","zone:deadwind","subzone:master-s-cellar"},src={"Archmage Leryda"}}
E["npc:mage-darius"] = {t="npc",n="Mage Darius",z="deadwind",s="Mage Darius is an emissary stationed outside the looming gates of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Representing the Violet Eye, he monitors the magical disruptions emanating from Medivh's ancient sanctuary.",h="Mage Darius is an emissary stationed outside the looming gates of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass.",sec={{t="Watcher at the Gates",b="Standing before the ominous threshold of Karazhan, Mage Darius serves as an outpost observer for the Violet Eye, a secretive sect of Kirin Tor spellcasters dedicated to monitoring Medivh's enigmatic tower. Deadwind Pass is a desolate, haunted corridor of twisted magic, and Darius keeps a wary vigil against the chaotic forces churning within the fortress walls.",sp=0},{t="The Violet Eye's Task",b="The Kirin Tor has long feared the lingering sorceries inside Karazhan following the demise of the Last Guardian. Darius acts as a field contact for intrepid adventurers braving the pass, evaluating those capable of resisting the arcane taint and rewarding allies who assist the Violet Eye in containing the tower's restless threats.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mage Darius?",a="Darius is a human spellcaster stationed outside Karazhan in Deadwind Pass, acting on behalf of the Violet Eye to observe the tower and aid travelers who assist their investigation.",al={"who is darius","apprentice darius","mage darius lore"}},{q="What is the Violet Eye?",a="The Violet Eye is a dedicated, secretive contingent of the Kirin Tor formed specifically to spy on Karazhan and safeguard Azeroth from the perilous magical anomalies left behind by Medivh.",al={"violet eye","who are the violet eye","kirin tor violet eye"}},{q="Why is Darius standing in Deadwind Pass?",a="He maintains an encampment right outside Karazhan's gates to keep watch over the stronghold, study the unstable magical surges leaking out, and coordinate with adventurers investigating the ruins.",al={"why is darius outside karazhan","darius location deadwind","what is he doing here"}},{q="Is Darius affiliated with the Alliance or Horde?",a="As an operative of the Kirin Tor's Violet Eye, Darius focuses on neutralizing arcane perils rather than factional conflict, interacting with any capable adventurer regardless of Alliance or Horde ties.",al={"is darius alliance","is darius horde","can horde talk to darius"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a representative of the Violet Eye, Darius exemplifies Dalaran's enduring commitment to containing rogue sorceries and the dangerous fallout of Guardian Medivh's work."},kw={"apprentice darius","deadwind pass","karazhan","kirin tor","mage darius","medivh","violet eye"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind"},src={"Mage Darius"}}
E["subzone:abandoned-kirin-tor-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Abandoned Kirin Tor Camp",z="deadwind",s="Perched in the craggy hills of Deadwind Pass near the border of Duskwood, this desolate campsite once housed Dalaran scholars monitoring Karazhan. Today, it lies ruined and forgotten, haunted by wild magical apparitions drawn to its lingering ley energies.",h="Perched in the craggy hills of Deadwind Pass near the border of Duskwood, this desolate campsite once housed...",sec={{t="A Forgotten Watchpost",b="Long before the First War, members of the Kirin Tor established this small outpost in the high rocks overlooking Karazhan. They came to study the strange, reality-bending anomalies emanating from the tower of the Guardian Medivh. An inscribed ritual circle still marks the stony ground, surrounded by discarded wagons, crates, and decayed tents. Instead of mages, however, the pass's volatile magic has drawn volatile Arcane Hunters and mana-feeding scavengers that prowl the perimeter, feasting on whatever dormant power remains.",sp=0},{t="Disaster and Erasure",b="The camp was led by the Dalaran archmage Arrexis, who sought to anchor and stabilize the warped space around Karazhan. Encouraged into reckless overreach by Medivh—who secretly plotted against his peers—Arrexis tested warding rituals that tore open pathways to demonic entities. The catastrophic breach wiped out Arrexis and his apprentices. Horrified by the calamity and desperate to prevent another disaster, the Kirin Tor struck Arrexis's research and expedition from their official archives, abandoning the site to the elements and wild magical beasts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is this camp doing in Deadwind Pass?",a="Scholars from the Kirin Tor set up this base prior to the First War to observe Karazhan and investigate the magical distortions surrounding the Guardian's tower.",al={"kirin tor camp deadwind","why is dalaran here","who built this camp"}},{q="What happened to the mages who lived here?",a="Their leader, Archmage Arrexis, conducted dangerous warding rituals that breached planar boundaries and summoned hostile demonic forces. The entire research team was killed during the disaster.",al={"what happened to arrexis","why is it abandoned","who died here"}},{q="Why are there arcane creatures prowling the camp?",a="The disastrous rituals cracked open local leylines and left residual magical energy behind, which naturally attracts arcane hunters and wild mana-hungry scavengers.",al={"excited mana scavengers","arcane hunters","why are there magic dogs here"}},{q="Why doesn't Dalaran maintain or reclaim the post?",a="After the catastrophe, the Kirin Tor expunged all records of Arrexis and his experiments to prevent anyone from repeating his fatal work, completely disavowing and deserting the location.",al={"why did kirin tor leave it","kirin tor cover up"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For mages trained in Dalaran, this ruined camp stands as a stark warning against unchecked planar research and meddling with Karazhan's fragile spatial boundaries.",["class:Warlock"]="The lingering remnants of planar tears and disastrous warding rituals make this hill an ominous example of what happens when arcane casters reach blindly into the nether."},kw={"arcane hunters","arrexis","deadwind pass","karazhan","kirin tor","mana scavengers","medivh"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:medivh","zone:duskwood","topic:first-war"},src={"Abandoned Kirin Tor Camp"}}
E["subzone:alturus-sanctum"] = {t="subzone",n="Alturus' Sanctum",z="deadwind",s="Alturus' Sanctum is a hidden magical refuge accessed through the Master's Cellar beneath Karazhan. Used by Archmage Alturus of the Violet Eye, it serves as an arcane workshop for studying the disturbed magical currents of Deadwind Pass.",h="Alturus' Sanctum is a hidden magical refuge accessed through the Master's Cellar beneath Karazhan.",sec={{t="A Hidden Workshop in the Shadows",b="Tucked away behind a shimmering gateway in the Master's Cellar, Alturus' Sanctum offers a rare sanctuary in the desolate expanse of Deadwind Pass. Within its chamber, Archmage Alturus—an operative of the secretive Violet Eye—conducts delicate research shielded from Karazhan's chaotic energies. During his apprenticeship under Medivh, a young Khadgar would visit Alturus here to collaborate on an artifact given to him by Archmage Antonidas: a fragment of the Archmage's Prismatic Disc. Shielded and windowless, the sanctum remains disconnected from the corrupted soil outside, serving solely as a base for observing the tower's restless magic.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Alturus' Sanctum located?",a="The sanctum is entered via a portal tucked inside the Master's Cellar, an underground complex beneath Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Because the chamber lacks windows and is entirely self-contained, its true physical location in Azeroth remains unknown.",al={"how to get to alturus sanctum","alturus sanctum location","where is it"}},{q="Who is Archmage Alturus?",a="Archmage Alturus is a high-ranking mage of Dalaran and a prominent member of the Violet Eye. His primary duty is to monitor Karazhan and investigate the lingering anomalies left behind by the Guardian Medivh.",al={"who is alturus","archmage alturus lore","who lives here"}},{q="What is the Violet Eye?",a="The Violet Eye is a clandestine sect within the Kirin Tor. Established to keep a watchful eye on Medivh and the magical disturbances surrounding Karazhan, its agents study the tower's fluctuating ley lines and ancient relics.",al={"violet eye","who are the violet eye","kirin tor spies"}},{q="Why did Khadgar visit this sanctum?",a="While studying as Medivh's apprentice, Khadgar met with Alturus here to examine a fragment of the Archmage's Prismatic Disc, a potent relic entrusted to Khadgar by Archmage Antonidas of Dalaran.",al={"khadgar alturus","khadgar visit","prismatic disc"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the sanctum represents the quiet vigilance of the Kirin Tor, demonstrating how high-ranking mages manipulate portals and ley energy right under the shadow of Medivh's tower."},kw={"alturus","antonidas","deadwind pass","karazhan","khadgar","master's cellar","prismatic disc","sanctum","violet eye"},rel={"npc:archmage-alturus","subzone:master-s-cellar","subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:medivh"},src={"Alturus' Sanctum"}}
E["subzone:ariden-s-camp"] = {t="subzone",n="Ariden's Camp",z="deadwind",s="Ariden's Camp is an abandoned encampment nestled just north of the path threading through Deadwind Pass. Left decaying in the shadow of Karazhan, it stands as an eerie, quiet anomaly amidst the desolate canyon winds. Travelers between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows often pass it with unease, unaware of the cursed peddler who once pitched his tent here.",h="Ariden's Camp is an abandoned encampment nestled just north of the path threading through Deadwind Pass.",sec={{t="A Silent Encampment",b="Tucked against the crags north of the gorge road connecting Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows, this dilapidated campsite looks like an ordinary transient stop long forsaken by living men. Yet in the oppressive gloom of Deadwind Pass, nothing remains unmarred by dark sorcery. The camp belonged to a peddler named Ariden, who brazenly attempted to hawk forged magical trinkets and curios claimed to have come from the tower of Medivh. Whatever fortune he sought in Karazhan's orbit was swallowed by the pass's lingering horrors, leaving only weathered cloth, cold ashes, and an enduring mystery.",sp=0},{t="The Peddler's Folly",b="Ariden was not merely an unlucky vagrant, but a grifter whose deceit unraveled terribly in the vicinity of the Guardian's seat. His hubris in profiting from Karazhan's sinister name drew a grim fate down upon him and his cohort, binding him to the very valley he sought to exploit as the leader of the spectral Dark Riders. The decaying remnants of his shelter stand undisturbed, a mundane tombstone marking where mortal avarice collided with forces far beyond mortal reckoning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Ariden's Camp located?",a="Ariden's Camp is located in Deadwind Pass, situated just north of the main road that links Duskwood in the west to the Swamp of Sorrows in the east, not far from Karazhan.",al={"aridens camp location","where is ariden camp","deadwind pass camp"}},{q="Who was Ariden?",a="Ariden was an unscrupulous merchant and peddler who established this camp to sell fake artifacts attributed to Medivh, the Last Guardian. His reckless greed ultimately doomed him to a dreadful curse, binding him as the leader of the terrifying Dark Riders of Karazhan.",al={"who is ariden","ariden lore","ariden backstory"},sp=2},{q="Why is the camp abandoned?",a="The camp was abandoned after Ariden and his associates fell victim to the dark, supernatural energies surrounding Deadwind Pass. Instead of walking the camp as living men, they were transformed into wandering, cursed spirits compelled to hunt real relics.",al={"why is aridens camp empty","what happened to the camp","who left aridens camp"},sp=1},{q="Are there any active threats at the camp right now?",a="The immediate clearing of the camp is quiet and eerily still, though Deadwind Pass itself is prowled by deadly deadwind ogres, spectral apparitions, and the foul winged beasts that roost near Karazhan.",al={"is aridens camp dangerous","mobs at aridens camp"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For scholars of the arcane, the ruined camp is an unsettling reminder of the hubris surrounding Karazhan; meddling with the legacy of Medivh rarely leaves charlatans unscathed.",["class:Rogue"]="A con artist setting up shop to peddle counterfeit relics beneath the most terrifying spire in the Eastern Kingdoms is either extraordinarily ambitious or remarkably foolish."},kw={"ariden","ariden's camp","dark riders","deadwind pass","duskwood","karazhan","medivh","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan","topic:dark-riders","topic:medivh","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows"},src={"Ariden's Camp"}}
E["subzone:deadman-s-crossing"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadman's Crossing",z="deadwind",s="Deadman's Crossing is an ominous junction set within the bleak canyon of Deadwind Pass. Branching between Duskwood, the Swamp of Sorrows, and the haunted tower of Karazhan, it serves as a grim threshold marked by gallows and warning signs. Despite its gruesome appearance, the path remains a vital thoroughfare for travelers moving across the southern Eastern Kingdoms.",h="Deadman's Crossing is an ominous junction set within the bleak canyon of Deadwind Pass.",sec={{t="A Grim Intersection",b="Situated near the western entrance of Deadwind Pass, Deadman's Crossing links the shadows of Duskwood with the murky depths of the Swamp of Sorrows, while a foreboding southern track ascends toward the haunted tower of Karazhan. The crossing takes its name from the twisted hangman's tree planted at the road's fork, where a pair of rotting corpses dangle overhead as a stark warning to all who pass. Beside the tree, battered wooden signs offer blunt advice to travelers, urging them to turn back and abandon hope. The canyon itself is thick with hostile beasts and dark sorceries, yet travelers moving steadfastly along the packed dirt road will find the crossing itself oddly unmolested, so long as they do not wander into the blighted rocks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does each road lead from Deadman's Crossing?",a="Heading west takes you out of the pass into the haunted woods of Duskwood. Heading east leads directly into the marshes of the Swamp of Sorrows. Following the winding southern path takes you deep into the heart of Deadwind Pass toward the cursed ruins and grand tower of Karazhan.",al={"where do roads go","crossing directions","deadmans crossing paths"}},{q="Who are the corpses hanging from the tree?",a="Their identities are lost to history. Deadwind Pass has claimed countless unfortunate wanderers, bandits, and refugees over the years, and someone erected the gallows tree as a gruesome boundary marker to warn away prospective travelers.",al={"hanging bodies","dead bodies on tree","who was hanged"}},{q="Is Deadman's Crossing safe for travelers?",a="Surprisingly, yes. While the surrounding crags and caves of Deadwind Pass teem with vicious vultures, ghosts, and ogres, the immediate crossing and the main east-west road remain clear. Low-level couriers and adventurers can safely pass through between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows, provided they never stray off the beaten dirt path.",al={"is it safe","will i get attacked on the road","danger level"}},{q="What do the signs at the crossing say?",a="The weathered wooden signposts offer ominous cautions: one bluntly instructs travelers to 'Turn Back!', while another warns 'Abandon hope, all ye who enter here,' leaving no doubt about the perilous nature of the valley.",al={"crossing signpost","what do signs read","abandon hope sign"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance couriers traveling from Darkshire to the outpost of Nethergarde Keep in the Blasted Lands, passing Deadman's Crossing is the quickest, albeit most unnerving, route.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde wanderers crossing westward from Stonard toward Duskwood must pass this grim landmark, providing an early taste of the blighted human lands ahead."},kw={"deadman's crossing","deadwind pass","duskwood","gallows","hangman's tree","karazhan","signpost","swamp of sorrows"},rel={"zone:deadwind","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Deadman's Crossing"}}
E["subzone:forgotten-crypt"] = {t="subzone",n="Forgotten Crypt",z="deadwind",s="Tucked away behind the ominous tower of Karazhan, the Forgotten Crypt sits within the overgrown graveyard of Morgan's Plot. Heavy iron bars seal its dark maw, shielding whatever lurks beneath Deadwind Pass from the light of day. It remains one of the most unsettling, impenetrable mysteries in the kingdom.",h="Tucked away behind the ominous tower of Karazhan, the Forgotten Crypt sits within the overgrown graveyard of...",sec={{t="A Sealed Chamber Beneath the Pass",b="Behind the spectral haunt of Karazhan lies Morgan's Plot, a desolate patch of burial ground where the weathered mausoleum of the Forgotten Crypt stands. Unlike the catacombs directly burrowed into the tower's foundation, this subterranean tomb sprawls deep into the earth. Sturdy iron gates bar curious travelers from peering too deep into its subterranean stairs. Locals avoid it entirely, whispered warnings cautioning that the depths beneath Deadwind Pass harbor horrors best kept buried from living eyes.",sp=0},{t="Whispers of the Deep Vaults",b="Those brave or foolish enough to press their faces against the grating speak of a freezing chill emanating from the stone passages. Though completely abandoned and sealed off from common entry, distant sounds of stagnant water and decaying timbers echo up from the dark. Some believe these vaults were constructed alongside Karazhan itself to inter those cursed or altered by Medivh's volatile sorcery, while others wonder if it was intended as a final resting place for the unfortunate souls claimed by the pass.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forgotten Crypt located?",a="The Forgotten Crypt is located in Deadwind Pass, situated in the graveyard known as Morgan's Plot just south and behind the tower of Karazhan.",al={"forgotten crypt location","where is the crypt in deadwind pass","how to find forgotten crypt"}},{q="Can you go inside the crypt?",a="No. The entrance is securely gated and locked off. Whatever rests within its sprawling subterranean tunnels remains completely sealed from normal entry.",al={"is the forgotten crypt open","can you enter forgotten crypt","how to get into forgotten crypt"}},{q="Is the Forgotten Crypt part of Karazhan?",a="It is distinct from the tower itself and from the catacombs dug directly beneath Karazhan's foundation, although its location in Morgan's Plot places it directly in the shadow of Medivh's ancient seat of power.",al={"karazhan crypts connection","is it part of karazhan"}},{q="Why is the crypt abandoned?",a="Few records remain of its original construction. It was likely built as a sprawling tomb for the surrounding region, but was ultimately abandoned and barred shut as Karazhan's corruption overtook Deadwind Pass.",al={"who built forgotten crypt","why was it sealed"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The crypt radiates a palpable aura of misery and ancient necromancy, drawing the curiosity of practitioners eager to commune with whatever residual suffering clings to its barred halls.",["class:Priest"]="The utter absence of the Light within the unhallowed grounds of Morgan's Plot makes this sealed tomb a deeply foreboding monument to desecration."},kw={"catacombs","cemetery","deadwind pass","forgotten crypt","karazhan","morgans plot","tomb","upside-down sinners"},rel={"subzone:morgan-s-plot","subzone:karazhan","subzone:karazhan-catacombs","zone:deadwind","zone:duskwood","subzone:tranquil-gardens-cemetery"},src={"Forgotten Crypt"}}
E["subzone:karazhan"] = {t="subzone",n="Karazhan",z="deadwind",s="Karazhan is the ominous, secluded tower standing at the southern end of Deadwind Pass. Once the sanctum of Medivh, the Last Guardian of Tirisfal, the citadel sits atop a potent convergence of ley lines that warps time, space, and reality around it. Though Medivh was slain during the First War, the abandoned fortress still hums with volatile arcane energy, restless spirits, and hidden dangers.",h="Karazhan is the ominous, secluded tower standing at the southern end of Deadwind Pass.",sec={{t="The Guardian's Spire",b="Long before the First War, the tower of Karazhan was raised upon ground shaped like a human skull, situated at a massive nexus of mystical ley lines. It served as a secluded refuge and repository of untold magical secrets for the Guardian Aegwynn and later her son, Medivh. Within its curving halls, Medivh lived alongside his loyal castellan Moroes, entertaining noble guests and housing an immense archive of arcane texts and relics that eclipsed even the libraries of the Kirin Tor. Yet the tower was also the stage for Azeroth's greatest betrayal, as Medivh fell under the demonic possession of Sargeras and secretly orchestrated the opening of the Dark Portal.",sp=0},{t="A Haunted Threshold",b="Following Medivh's death at the hands of Anduin Lothar and his apprentice Khadgar, Karazhan sealed its gates and was left to decay. However, the tower has never truly slept. Its intersection of potent ley lines continues to warp the fabric of reality, casting ghostly echoes, illusions, and temporal distortions across Deadwind Pass. Rumors persist that an evil presence has begun stirring inside the quiet fortress once more, and strange entities—including the shadowy Dark Riders who scour the surrounding lands for forgotten relics—are inexorably drawn to its towering silhouette.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built Karazhan?",a="Karazhan was constructed roughly six centuries before the First War by Aegwynn, the Magna of the Council of Tirisfal. Seeking a secluded refuge away from the prying eyes of the Kirin Tor and the Council, she tapped into a powerful nexus of ley lines in Deadwind Pass to siphon energy for her magical wards.",al={"who made karazhan","karazhan creator","origin of karazhan"}},{q="Who was Medivh, and why did he live here?",a="Medivh was the son of Aegwynn and the Last Guardian of Tirisfal, charged with defending Azeroth from demonic threats. He made Karazhan his primary home and sanctuary, surrounding himself with vast stores of arcane knowledge, servants like Moroes, and lavish gatherings to mask his descent into madness.",al={"who lived in karazhan","medivh lore","the last guardian"}},{q="What happened to Medivh in the tower?",a="Unbeknownst to the world, Medivh had been possessed since birth by the spirit of the Dark Titan Sargeras. Under this demonic influence, he used the tower's magic to contact the warlock Gul'dan and open the Dark Portal. Discovering his treachery, his apprentice Khadgar, Lord Anduin Lothar, and the half-orc Garona infiltrated Karazhan and slew the Guardian, ending his corruption.",al={"how did medivh die","medivh death","fall of medivh"}},{q="Can you enter Karazhan right now?",a="No. The main gates and threshold of the tower remain tightly sealed and warded against intruders. While travelers can wander the abandoned village, crumbling church, and shadowy subterranean cellars surrounding the grounds, the spire itself is shut tight.",al={"can i go inside karazhan","is karazhan open","entering karazhan"}},{q="Why is the area around Karazhan so corrupted and dead?",a="Karazhan sits at an ancient epicenter of magical violence where the fabric of reality was torn open, long before the tower was built. Combined with the massive concentration of raw ley energy flowing beneath it and the dark demonic sorceries Medivh unleashed inside, the surrounding canyon withered into the desolate wasteland known as Deadwind Pass.",al={"why is deadwind pass dead","karazhan curse","why deadwind pass empty"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders connected to the tower?",a="The Dark Riders are spectral figures created when Medivh cursed a band of charlatan merchants who attempted to sell him fraudulent magical trinkets. Bound by his powerful curse, the riders are condemned to scour the lands and retrieve powerful, genuine magical artifacts to bring back to the tower.",al={"what are the dark riders","riders of deadwind pass","karazhan riders"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Karazhan is a monument to the heights and perils of mortal sorcery. It houses an unmatched collection of artifacts and writings once kept out of the hands of the Kirin Tor, though its unstable ley lines threaten to consume any careless practitioner.",["faction:Alliance"]="The tower holds tragic significance for the kingdom of Stormwind. It was the home of Medivh—boyhood friend of King Llane Wrynn and Anduin Lothar—whose betrayal from within these walls unleashed the First War upon humanity."},kw={"aegwynn","dark riders","deadwind pass","guardian","karazhan","khadgar","medivh","moroes","sargeras","tirisfal"},rel={"topic:medivh","zone:deadwind","topic:anduin-lothar","subzone:dark-portal","topic:first-war","topic:sargeras","topic:dark-riders","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Karazhan"}}
E["subzone:karazhan-catacombs"] = {t="subzone",n="Karazhan Catacombs",z="deadwind",s="The Karazhan Catacombs are an expansive subterranean network carved beneath the foundations of Medivh's ancient tower in Deadwind Pass. Cloaked in dark magical residue and ominous silence, the vaults serve as the secluded base of operations for the mysterious Dark Riders and hoard countless stolen artifacts.",h="The Karazhan Catacombs are an expansive subterranean network carved beneath the foundations of Medivh's...",sec={{t="The Vaults Beneath the Tower",b="Burrowed deep into the bedrock of Deadwind Pass directly below the tower of Karazhan, these cavernous catacombs are entered through an iron gate near the structure's base. The subterranean chambers mirror the strange, reality-bending aura of Medivh's former home. Long isolated from the rest of the kingdom, the winding corridors hold damp vaults, restless phantasms, and ancient masonry, all shadowed by the lingering taint of the Guardian's tragic fall.",sp=0},{t="Lair of the Dark Riders",b="The catacombs have gained a sinister reputation as the primary refuge of the Dark Riders—the spectral, hooded figures that terrorize nearby Duskwood and Deadwind Pass. Led by Ariden, these grim hunters ride across the countryside in search of powerful, ancient relics to drag back into the darkness. Within these halls lie stockpiles of stolen armaments, cursed curiosities, and enigmatic artifacts hoarded away from the eyes of the living world.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are the Karazhan Catacombs?",a="They are a massive network of underground chambers and vaults resting directly beneath the tower of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass, accessible via a gated entrance at the tower's base.",al={"karazhan catacombs","tunnels under karazhan","crypts beneath medivh"}},{q="Who lives inside these catacombs?",a="The catacombs primarily harbor the Dark Riders, their shadowy steeds, and wandering phantasms and cursed guardians tethered to the tower's restless magical currents.",al={"who is down there","catacomb inhabitants","monsters in karazhan catacombs"}},{q="Why do the Dark Riders gather here?",a="The Dark Riders use the remote, spell-cloaked halls as a secure sanctuary and treasury, bringing relics and artifacts plundered from travelers across the Eastern Kingdoms into the deep chambers.",al={"dark rider base","why dark riders","what do dark riders do here"}},{q="Is this the same place as the Forgotten Crypt?",a="No. The catacombs sit directly beneath the tower itself, while the infamous Forgotten Crypt lies nearby beneath the graveyard of Morgan's Plot.",al={"forgotten crypt","morgans plot crypt","karazhan crypts difference"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the catacombs thrum with volatile residual energy and the eerie magical fallout of Medivh's doomed reign as Guardian.",["faction:Alliance"]="The artifacts hauled into these subterranean vaults are often plundered from innocent travelers and homesteads across Duskwood and Stormwind's southern reaches."},kw={"ariden","catacombs","dark riders","deadwind","karazhan","medivh","vaults"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:dark-riders","topic:medivh","subzone:forgotten-crypt","subzone:morgan-s-plot","zone:duskwood","topic:sargeras"},src={"Karazhan Catacombs"}}
E["subzone:karazhan-raid"] = {t="subzone",n="Karazhan (raid)",z="deadwind",s="Karazhan is the towering citadel of Medivh, the last Guardian of Tirisfal, situated at the southern edge of Deadwind Pass. Following Medivh's fall during the First War, the citadel was sealed off from the world, leaving its halls haunted by restless spirits, unbound magic, and encroaching demonic forces.",h="Karazhan is the towering citadel of Medivh, the last Guardian of Tirisfal, situated at the southern edge of...",sec={{t="The Haunted Spire",b="Built upon an ancient focal point of telluric energy in Deadwind Pass, Karazhan was once the seat of the Guardian Medivh. Following his demise, the fortress became an echo chamber of tragic history. Its lower reaches house phantom banquets, spectral stables, and an automated theatrical stage where illusions repeat endlessly. Farther up, the tower unravels into an untamed spire of arcane menageries, forbidden libraries, and unstable spatial anomalies. Though its master is gone, the tower's enchanted defenses and twisted denizens remain active, guarding centuries of hoarded esoteric knowledge against any who dare seek entry.",sp=0},{t="A Beacon for the Nether",b="Karazhan's wards have steadily decayed since the First War, allowing foul intruders to breach its uppermost sanctums. Deep within the upper chambers and the dimensional rift of Netherspace, demonic agents and otherworldly entities have taken root, drawn by the lingering power of the Guardian. The tower's twisted geometry and unhinged magical reserves make it one of the most perilous sites in the Eastern Kingdoms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Karazhan?",a="Karazhan is the abandoned citadel of Medivh, the last Guardian of Tirisfal. Located in Deadwind Pass, it is an enormous mystical tower steeped in arcane power, now populated by lingering ghosts, constructs, and demonic interlopers.",al={"what is this place","karazhan lore","who lives in karazhan"}},{q="Can you enter Karazhan right now?",a="The tower remains sealed to ordinary travelers. Its gates are locked, though the magical emanations and disturbances surrounding its perimeter make it a prime point of interest for researchers and adventurers wandering Deadwind Pass.",al={"is karazhan open","how to get into karazhan","can i enter the tower"}},{q="Who was Medivh?",a="Medivh was the last Guardian of Tirisfal, chosen to safeguard Azeroth against demonic incursions. Corrupted by the Dark Titan Sargeras, he opened the Dark Portal and brought the orcish Horde into Azeroth before he was slain inside this very tower during the First War.",al={"medivh backstory","who is the guardian"}},{q="Why is the tower full of ghosts?",a="When Medivh died, the intense magical backlash and temporal distortions anchored the souls of his servants, guests, and retainers to the stone. Phantom revelers, stable hands, and stage actors endlessly repeat the routines of the tower's final days.",al={"why are there phantoms","spirits in karazhan"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="Karazhan represents the ultimate cautionary tale of unchecked arcane power and the towering legacy left behind by the last Guardian.",["class:Warlock"]="The planar fractures atop the tower offer a tantalizing glimpse of Twisting Nether incursions into Azeroth."},kw={"deadwind pass","guardian","karazhan","medivh","moroes","netherspace","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:medivh"},src={"Karazhan (raid)"}}
E["subzone:master-s-cellar"] = {t="subzone",n="Master's Cellar",z="deadwind",s="The Master's Cellar is a sprawling subterranean complex situated beneath the ruined settlement south of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Once serving Medivh's estate as wine cellars and storage vaults, it has descended into a haunted ruin teeming with the restless spectres of former servants and caretakers.",h="The Master's Cellar is a sprawling subterranean complex situated beneath the ruined settlement south of...",sec={{t="Haunted Underbelly of Karazhan",b="Just south of the imposing tower of Karazhan lie the ruined remnants of a hamlet that once housed the servants, groundskeepers, and attendants who maintained Medivh's estate. Beneath these crumbled homes sits the Master's Cellar. Accessible through two separate entrances in the surface ruins, the complex expands far underground. One doorway opens into an extensive vaulted wine cellar, while the other descends through collapsed stonework into deep natural caverns. Whatever dark demise befell Karazhan and its master swallowed this basement as well, leaving the unliving remnants of caretakers, wailing spectres, and damned souls trapped in endless servitude.",sp=0},{t="The Lower Caverns",b="The deepest recesses of the complex, designated the Lower Cellar, reveal that Medivh's excavations breached the raw subterranean rock of Deadwind Pass. The cellar's foundations crumbled into these cavern systems, creating a jagged labyrinth that echoes with ghostly wails. While adventurers exploring the Pass rarely find living souls here, the pervasive magical corruption leaking from the nearby tower has firmly anchored these apparitions to the stone, making the caverns as perilous as the ruins above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Master's Cellar originally used for?",a="It served as the primary storage vaults and wine cellars for the tower of Karazhan. The village above housed the domestic staff and groundskeepers who maintained the Guardian Medivh's sprawling household, using the subterranean vaults to store provisions and vintage kegs.",al={"purpose of masters cellar","what is this cellar","why is there a wine cellar here"}},{q="Why is the cellar full of ghosts?",a="When Medivh succumbed to corruption and met his end within Karazhan, a disastrous wave of magical fallout scourged the surrounding pass. The servants, staff, and villagers living in the hamlet were wiped out, their spirits bound to the dark ruins as restless phantoms and unliving caretakers.",al={"why are there ghosts","who are the undead in the cellar","why is masters cellar haunted"}},{q="How do you access the cave systems below the cellar?",a="There are two distinct cellar doorways among the ruined buildings south of Karazhan. While the eastern entrance leads into the structured wine cellar, the western entryway descends into a collapsed section of masonry that drops down into the natural underground caves of the Lower Cellar.",al={"how to get into the lower cellar","masters cellar entrances","where is the cave entrance"}},{q="Is the Master's Cellar directly connected to the interior of Karazhan?",a="No. Despite its proximity to the base of the tower and its historical role in provisioning the Guardian's estate, the subterranean chambers do not offer an open passage into Karazhan itself. The cellar remains self-contained beneath the village ruins.",al={"does masters cellar lead into karazhan","entrance to karazhan from cellar"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The ghostly remnants lingering beneath the Guardian's estate bear testament to the severe arcane backlash unleashed when Medivh fell, turning ordinary domestic vaults into a nexus of lingering spectral energy.",["class:Priest"]="The tormented spectres trapped within the damp vaults are the tragic souls of simple caretakers and servants, denied peace by the lingering curse on Deadwind Pass."},kw={"deadwind pass","karazhan","lower cellar","master's cellar","masters cellar","medivh","unliving caretaker"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Master's Cellar"}}
E["subzone:morgan-s-plot"] = {t="subzone",n="Morgan's Plot",z="deadwind",s="Morgan's Plot is a desolate burial ground and crumbling chapel tucked away just behind the tower of Karazhan in Deadwind Pass. Dominated by restless undead and brooding silence, it holds the forgotten crypts and final resting places of those once tied to Medivh's domain.",h="Morgan's Plot is a desolate burial ground and crumbling chapel tucked away just behind the tower of Karazhan...",sec={{t="A Grave in the Shadow of the Tower",b="Nestled against the sheer rocky slopes directly behind Karazhan, Morgan's Plot is a sorrowful, overgrown cemetery centered on a ruined chapel and underground crypts. Long before the land decayed into Deadwind Pass, the estate served the burial needs of the tower's inhabitants and nearby grounds. Following the downfall of the Last Guardian, Medivh, dark energies seeped into the earth, driving away all normalcy. Today, restless unliving wander the chapel grounds, haunting the headstones of servants and historic figures alike.",sp=0},{t="Resting Place of Guardians and Servants",b="Beneath the crooked tombstones and inside the subterranean catacombs lie the remains of several figures tied intimately to Karazhan's history. Medivh's mother, the former Guardian Aegwynn, laid the bodies of Medivh, his seneschal Moroes, and their cook to rest here following the tragedy that shattered the tower. While mysteries linger as to what truly remains in the crypts beneath the soil, the soil itself feels heavy with old, lingering arcana and unquiet spirits.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Morgan's Plot located?",a="Morgan's Plot lies in southern Deadwind Pass, situated in a gloomy hollow directly behind the high spire of Karazhan.",al={"where is morgans plot","morgans plot location","how to get to morgans plot"}},{q="Who is buried here?",a="Historically, the graveyard and crypts served Karazhan's household. Following Medivh's fall, his mother Aegwynn buried the Guardian here alongside his loyal seneschal Moroes and the tower's cook.",al={"who is buried at morgans plot","medivh grave","moroes grave","aegwynn burial"}},{q="What threats can be found at Morgan's Plot?",a="The chapel and surrounding grounds are haunted by unliving residents and restless spirits that linger around the gravestones and the entrance to the crypt.",al={"morgans plot mobs","what enemies are here","chapel monsters"}},{q="Who is Lydia Accoste?",a="Lydia Accoste is a lone human woman who can be encountered lingering near the abandoned, overgrown chapel grounds despite the surrounding dangers.",al={"lydia accoste","npc at morgans plot"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="The defiled graves and roaming unliving residents make Morgan's Plot a stark reminder of the corrupting taint that lingers wherever the Guardian's dark fate unfolded.",["class:Mage"]="Mages of Dalaran regard this place with quiet dread, knowing it holds the burial soil chosen by Aegwynn to inter those struck down during Medivh's tragic end."},kw={"aegwynn","crypt","deadwind pass","karazhan","lydia accoste","medivh","morgan's plot","morgans plot","moroes"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","zone:deadwind","topic:medivh","topic:burning-legion"},src={"Morgan's Plot"}}
E["subzone:vice"] = {t="subzone",n="Vice",z="deadwind",s="The Vice is a rugged, desolate expanse of Deadwind Pass situated along the road leading toward Karazhan. It serves as the territory of the Deadwind ogres, who maintain rough mounds and scattered camps in defiance of the land's grim isolation. Travelers passing through must navigate both their crude brutality and their surprisingly adept wielders of dark magic.",h="The Vice is a rugged, desolate expanse of Deadwind Pass situated along the road leading toward Karazhan.",sec={{t="A Desolate Stronghold",b="Stretching across the southern stretches of Deadwind Pass, the Vice is defined by barren earth, jagged rock faces, and crude mounds erected by the Deadwind ogre clan. While the surrounding canyon is largely abandoned to vengeful ghosts and scavenger vultures, these ogres have carved out a stubborn foothold directly beside the main path approaching Karazhan. Why they chose such a bleak and magically scarred waste remains an enduring mystery, but any traveler passing between Duskwood and the Swamp of Sorrows quickly learns they defend their camps with fierce territorial violence.",sp=0},{t="Brute Force and Dark Arts",b="Unlike mere highwaymen, the ogres dwelling in the Vice possess both heavy martial strength and dangerous arcane talent. Alongside hulking bruisers, Deadwind warlocks practice crude yet lethal fel sorceries among the earthen mounds. Their presence so close to the abandoned seat of Medivh suggests a hunger for residual magical power, making the canyon a lethal gauntlet for wandering scholars and solitary scouts alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Vice?",a="The Vice is a rugged subzone in southern Deadwind Pass, characterized by earthen mounds, scattered campfires, and rocky ravines controlled entirely by the Deadwind ogres.",al={"the vice deadwind","what is vice","vice area deadwind pass"}},{q="Why are the ogres living here?",a="Nobody knows for certain why the ogres chose to settle in such an inhospitable, haunted gorge. Their warlocks may be drawn to the lingering arcane fallout emanating from nearby Karazhan, or they may simply exploit the remote mountain road to prey upon passing travelers.",al={"why ogres in deadwind","deadwind ogre motive","why are ogres at the vice"}},{q="Where does the road through the Vice lead?",a="The trail traversing the Vice winds deeper into the crags of southern Deadwind Pass, leading straight toward the ominous gates of Karazhan, the abandoned tower of the Guardian Medivh.",al={"vice road destination","where does the road go","path through vice"}},{q="What dangers should travelers expect in the Vice?",a="Travelers will encounter aggressive Deadwind ogres patrolling the road and defending their mounds. In addition to physically imposing brawlers, the clan includes dangerous warlocks who wield curses and shadow magic.",al={"vice threats","enemies in vice","what attacks you in the vice"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The Deadwind ogres inhabiting the Vice display an unexpected mastery of dark magic, suggesting that even isolated brute clans can tap into corruptive fel energies.",["class:Mage"]="The ogres' presence along the direct approach to Karazhan raises questions for the Kirin Tor regarding whether residual energies from Medivh's tower are influencing the local beasts and clans."},kw={"deadwind ogres","deadwind pass","deadwind warlocks","karazhan","ogre mounds","vice"},rel={"zone:deadwind","subzone:karazhan"},src={"Vice"}}
E["topic:dark-riders"] = {t="topic",n="Dark Riders",z="deadwind",s="The Dark Riders are a band of cursed, hooded horsemen who terrorize Deadwind Pass and Duskwood. Bound by an ancient affliction to harvest powerful relics for Karazhan, they hunt magic ruthlessly and leave only slaughter in their wake.",h="The Dark Riders are a band of cursed, hooded horsemen who terrorize Deadwind Pass and Duskwood.",sec={{t="The Curse of the Guardian",b="Before their eternal hunt began, the Dark Riders were unscrupulous traveling merchants led by a man named Ariden. They made the fatal mistake of attempting to swindle the Guardian Medivh with counterfeit magical trinkets. Possessed by Sargeras, the sorcerer punished their deceit with a grim fate: to wander the kingdom forever, bound to seek out genuine magical relics and haul them back to the vaults beneath Karazhan. Harsh, shrill, and nearly impossible to track, the Riders remain invisible until they choose to strike.",sp=0},{t="Slaughter at the Farmstead",b="The Riders recently surged into Duskwood, drawn by space-warping tremors radiating from the Scythe of Elune. Unbeknownst to them, the miner Jitters had uncovered and promptly lost the ancient staff inside Roland's Doom. Tracking the magical signature to the nearby Yorgen Farmstead, the Riders demanded the artifact from Sven Yorgen's family. When the terrified settlers could give no answers, the horsemen butchered Sven's wife and children in cold blood, driving Sven into a vengeful madness.",sp=1},{t="Shadows over Deadwind",b="Operating out of Ariden's Camp in the shadow of Karazhan, the Riders have struck targets across the Eastern Kingdoms, even breaching the protective dome over Dalaran to loot its vaults. Whispers in Duskwood also link their sinister hunts to the rogue necromancer Morbent Fel. Though feared as invincible phantoms, those who glimpse behind their cloaks have witnessed not undead monsters, but the tormented faces of terrified men helplessly trapped in servitude to their master.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the Dark Riders?",a="They were once dishonest merchants who tried to sell fake magical items to the sorcerer Medivh. Cursed by Medivh, they are bound to scour the world for genuine, powerful magical relics and bring them back to Karazhan.",al={"black riders","what are the dark riders","who are the riders in duskwood"}},{q="What did they do to Sven Yorgen's family?",a="They were hunting the Scythe of Elune, which had been unearthed nearby. When they interrogated Sven Yorgen's wife and children and found they knew nothing about the artifact, the Riders murdered them without mercy.",al={"sven farm massacre","what happened at yorgen farmstead","why did riders kill svens family"},sp=1},{q="Who is Ariden?",a="Ariden was the leader of the traveling merchants who attempted to con Medivh. He now leads the Dark Riders on their cursed hunts from Ariden's Camp in Deadwind Pass.",al={"leader of dark riders","ariden","aridans camp"}},{q="Why are the Dark Riders in Duskwood?",a="They were drawn to the dark forest by the temporal and magical disturbances caused when Jitters unearthed the Scythe of Elune in Roland's Doom.",al={"why are dark riders in duskwood","dark riders scythe of elune","what are they hunting"},sp=1},{q="Are the Dark Riders undead?",a="The exact nature of Medivh's curse remains unclear. While they possess supernatural stealth and shrieking voices, those who have peered beneath their enchanted cloaks have reported seeing the faces of terrified, living men bound against their will.",al={"are dark riders ghosts","are the dark riders undead","what are dark riders made of"}},{q="Are they working with Morbent Fel?",a="The Night Watch has noted suspicious dealings between the Dark Riders and the necromancer Morbent Fel in Duskwood, though the exact terms of their alliance remain unknown.",al={"morbent fel and dark riders","morbent fel alliance"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The Dark Riders' ruthless hunt for the Scythe of Elune poses a severe threat to the balance, as the weapon's feral energies can wreak havoc across Duskwood.",["faction:Alliance"]="Striking just beyond Stormwind's borders, the Riders slaughter innocent homesteaders like Sven Yorgen's family, proving how far the kingdom's frontier has slipped from its grasp.",["class:Mage"]="Created by Medivh's terrifying curse, the Riders are living warnings of Karazhan's tainted sorcery and have even breached Dalaran's magical warding."},kw={"ariden","black riders","dark riders","deadwind pass","duskwood","jitters","karazhan","medivh","scythe of elune","sven yorgen"},rel={"npc:sven-yorgen","npc:jitters","quest:95","subzone:ariden-s-camp","subzone:karazhan","quest:1043","quest:55","topic:medivh"},src={"Dark Riders"}}
E["zone:deadwind"] = {t="zone",n="Deadwind Pass",z="deadwind",s="Deadwind Pass is a blighted, jagged canyon in central Azeroth connecting Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows. At its center looms the Ivory Spire of Karazhan, former seat of the Guardian Medivh, whose death unleashed corrupting magical runoff across the land. It is a lifeless corridor stalked by ogres, ghosts, and demonic winds, offering neither refuge nor civilized shelter.",h="Deadwind Pass is a blighted, jagged canyon in central Azeroth connecting Duskwood to the Swamp of Sorrows.",sec={{t="A Canyon of Bones and Howling Wind",b="Once considered an extension of the Redridge Mountains, Deadwind Pass has devolved into a hollowed-out scar of bleached stone and petrified wood. A foul, relentless wind cuts through the ravines, giving the gorge its name. The sky above is locked in a perpetual sepulchral gray, threatening erratic lightning storms that make traveling with metal arms hazardous. Totemic effigies hang from lifeless branches alongside the main road, warning wayfarers to keep moving. There are no fertile soils here, no mineable mineral veins, and no towns or flight masters to offer aid.",sp=0},{t="The Legacy of Karazhan",b="The history of the pass revolves around the towering citadel of Karazhan. Built atop a potent convergence of subterranean ley lines, the tower served as the redoubt of the Guardian Medivh. It was within this spire that Medivh plotted the opening of the Dark Portal and the ruin of Stormwind. When his madness and possession came to light during the First War, an expedition led by Lord Anduin Lothar and young Khadgar breached the tower and executed him. Medivh's violent demise released a shockwave of fel taint that blighted both the pass and neighboring Brightwood, leaving Karazhan an ominous, locked husk leaking unstable magical energy.",sp=0},{t="Deadwind Ogres and Ruined Plots",b="South of the main thoroughfare, the pass branches into the territory of the Deadwind ogres around the Vice. Dressed in foul rags and wielding jagged iron, these brutes relentlessly ambuscade anyone venturing near the southern road, reportedly serving a hidden master within the vicinity. Further south lies Morgan's Plot and the skeletal remnants of a hamlet that once catered to the tower. Today, the village's above-ground ruins and labyrinthine cellars crawl with wailing phantoms and restless shades, remnants of those whose lives were extinguished by Karazhan's unbridled sorcery.",sp=0},{t="The Scythe and the Dark Riders",b="Long before the present year, a cabal of dishonest merchants led by a swindler named Ariden operated out of a camp in the northern canyon, attempting to sell counterfeit magical relics to Medivh. Displeased by their deception, the possessed Guardian inflicted a dark curse upon the traders, compelling them to scour the lands for authentic artifacts. Reborn as the cloaked Dark Riders, they have recently brought terror to Duskwood, slaughtering innocent homesteaders in a ruthless hunt for the enigmatic Scythe of Elune before retreating back into the shadows of the pass.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is this place so dead and ruined?",a="Deadwind Pass was ruined by the arcane pollution and dark sorcery centered on Karazhan. When the Guardian Medivh was slain in his tower during the First War, an explosion of fel magic cascaded down the ravine, petrifying the trees, stripping the earth of life, and permanently blighting the sky.",al={"why is deadwind pass dead","what happened to deadwind pass","why are trees dead here"}},{q="Are there any friendly towns, inns, or flight masters here?",a="No. Deadwind Pass features no friendly settlements, inns, or flight masters for either faction. Alliance travelers must rely on Darkshire in Duskwood to the west, while Horde members must stage out of Stonard in the Swamp of Sorrows to the east.",al={"deadwind pass flight path","is there a town in deadwind pass","deadwind pass inn"}},{q="Can I enter Karazhan right now?",a="The grand iron doors of Karazhan remain firmly barred. Whispers persist that a sinister power has taken up residence within the upper halls, but the tower is presently sealed, leaving its mysteries hidden behind locked gates and haunted foundations.",al={"is karazhan open","can you go inside karazhan","enter karazhan"}},{q="Who are the Dark Riders and where did they come from?",a="The Dark Riders originated from Ariden's Camp in northern Deadwind Pass. Formerly charlatans who tried to cheat Medivh with fake relics, they were cursed by the Guardian to scour Azeroth for genuine magical treasures—a grim mandate that recently led them into Duskwood to butcher farmers while hunting the Scythe of Elune.",al={"dark riders deadwind","ariden dark riders","scythe of elune riders"},sp=1},{q="Can I gather herbs or mine ore in Deadwind Pass?",a="No. The magical cataclysm completely leached the soil and rock of vitality. Useful medicinal herbs cannot take root in the desiccated dirt, and precious mineral veins do not form in the dead stone. The only native wildlife to survive are scavenger vultures.",al={"deadwind pass herbs","deadwind mining","deadwind pass resources"}},{q="Who lives in Deadwind Pass today?",a="The pass is primarily occupied by the aggressive Deadwind ogre clan inhabiting the Vice, along with lingering carrion birds and restless ghosts. A few wandering human scavengers survive on the move without Alliance support, while Kirin Tor agents watch the pass with unease.",al={"inhabitants of deadwind pass","who lives in deadwind","deadwind pass mobs"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The ley lines beneath Deadwind Pass converge directly into Karazhan. The Kirin Tor monitors this nexus with extreme dread, knowing how Medivh warped its arcane conduit to breach dimensional barriers.",["class:Warlock"]="Traces of raw demonic energy still coat the rocks and stone cellars. Medivh's possession and the necromantic history of the pass have left an indelible stain of fel magic waiting to be felt.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stormwind considers this dead corridor a grim scar on its borders. The horrors that escaped Karazhan ended Brightwood's splendor and continue to threaten Darkshire just down the western road.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers moving westward from Stonard, this canyon is a hostile bottleneck infested with vengeful human spirits and hulking ogres that attack anyone entering the gorge."},kw={"ariden","dark riders","deadman's crossing","deadwind ogres","deadwind pass","karazhan","medivh","morgan's plot","the last guardian","vice"},rel={"subzone:karazhan","topic:medivh","subzone:morgan-s-plot","subzone:ariden-s-camp","topic:dark-riders","zone:duskwood","zone:swampofsorrows","quest:1043"},src={"Deadwind Pass (Classic)","Deadwind Pass"}}
